@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+---
+title: "Seismoacoustic recovery of the SpaceX CRS-32 Dragon re-entry with a proof-of-concept for automated detection"
+collection: publications
+category: papers
+permalink: /publications/2026-seismoacoustic-spacex-crs32
+excerpt: 'Built on Dr. Fernando's Science-published work; implemented an end-to-end pipeline to detect and localize atmospheric re-entries using open-source seismic network data, with gradient-based contour mapping and ML-based automated phase picking.'
+date: 2026-01-01
+venue: 'Acta Astronautica (In Review)'
+paperurl: 'https://doi.org/10.31223/X50J66'
+---
+
+Yu, Mikel, and Fernando, Benjamin. *Seismoacoustic recovery of the SpaceX CRS-32 Dragon re-entry with a proof-of-concept for automated detection.* In review at *Acta Astronautica*. Preprint: [doi:10.31223/X50J66](https://doi.org/10.31223/X50J66).
+
+Built directly on Dr. Fernando's Science-published work. Implemented an end-to-end pipeline to detect and localize atmospheric re-entries using open-source seismic network data. Constructed a gradient-based contour mapping and predictive line fitting for trajectory triangulation. Fine-tuned a classification model on limited labelled data, achieving high accuracy on held-out examples, demonstrating promise for ML to automate seismic phase picking.
